:"2016-06-09T18:50:51-07:00","id":911349,"title":"","content":"So would it be a bad idea to make a discipline to allow vampires to hack them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:59:50-07:00","id":911358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910150-godmachine-infrastructures-and-vampires?p=911349#post911349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would it be a bad idea to make a discipline to allow vampires to hack them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all, if you want to do so, go for it. Now a Bloodline to look into would be the Lynx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:18:12-07:00","id":911370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910150-godmachine-infrastructures-and-vampires?p=910651#post910651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed I am.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Scarlet Plague is a good piece of Elimination Infrastructure, possibly one of the most resilient too, no attackable Linchpin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:12:45-07:00","id":911455,"title":"","content":"What if their form of hacking was temporally granting themselves boons like a demon can grant through pacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T01:51:18-07:00","id":912154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910150-godmachine-infrastructures-and-vampires?p=911349#post911349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would it be a bad idea to make a discipline to allow vampires to hack them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Biggest problems would be that a) there is no established system that determines the effects of a given project or how to achieve particular effects by hacking them*, and b) infrastructural projects in general can do damn near anything conceptually, though <i>individual</i> projects likely have constraints on what they can accomplish and at what cost, for which, again, there is no set system.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like proposing a power that can harness and alter the Dragon's Nests tended by the Ordo Dracul. The problem isn't that the Blood couldn't or shouldn't be able to do that somehow, it's... what does that mean? Dragon's Nests are all kinds of different things and lack universal definition, so you walk a line without clear guidance, between something so broad it outperforms anything else or something narrow and unsatisfyingly specific. The same applies to godhacking infrastructure. If you think you can walk that line and have a suitably vampiric way to express subverting God-Machine projects, go for it.<br /> <br /> <i>* Flowers of Hell advertises some infrastructural hacking rules, but I found them woefully lacking, a rare letdown in an otherwise solid book. They mostly boil down to ways to extract Aether, gather intelligence, or assess what the God-Machine is using the project to do, but very little on actually altering the output.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T02:15:02-07:00","id":913961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910150-godmachine-infrastructures-and-vampires?p=911349#post911349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would it be a bad idea to make a discipline to allow vampires to hack them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much a bad idea as a problematic one, as Infrastructure is pretty much a blanket term for all the weird shit God-Machine enacts and oversees. How do you hack a cemetery that keeps spawning fresh corpses in old graves? What's the benefit to the vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:00:30-07:00","id":915784,"title":"","content":"There are other options, you aren't limited to discipline here.<br /> <br /> Humans with unseen senses-godmachine can do it, according to god machine chronicles, so how about some stigmatic vampires?<br /> <br /> Or a bloodline with bloodline benefits along those lines?<br /> <br /> Or use the crafting rules from chronicles of darkness to allow them to build minor occult matrices. Sure, dice bonuses is rather tame, but make the descriptions weird- Bullets that change course in mid air as they scream their targets name, cockroach typewriters that write letters of hypnotic power, a houseplant that you plug its root into a computer to hack them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:19:18-07:00","id":916261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910150-godmachine-infrastructures-and-vampires?p=915784#post915784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There are other options, you aren't limited to discipline here.<br /> <br /> Humans with unseen senses-godmachine can do it, according to god machine chronicles, so how about some stigmatic vampires?<br /> <br /> Or a bloodline with bloodline benefits along those lines?<br /> <br /> Or use the crafting rules from chronicles of darkness to allow them to build minor occult matrices. Sure, dice bonuses is rather tame, but make the descriptions weird- Bullets that change course in mid air as they scream their targets name, cockroach typewriters that write letters of hypnotic power, a houseplant that you plug its root into a computer to hack them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kevorkiandoctor's idea, discussed in greater length on the Requiem board, is to give each Clan a &quot;magical&quot; Discipline, which they can choose instead of their usual signature Discipline (Majesty for Daeva, Dominate for Ventrue etc) to give each clan its own brand of mysticism. So, while you are generally right, in this case he actually is limited to a Discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T13:30:12-07:00","id":916397,"title":"","content":"I think more important is what do u imagine a vampire doing with it. <br /> Hacking it in what way? A vampire could study one and learn how it works (yeah it might take years though) and use it. Humans in the setting have. Do I guess the first level would let u see infrastructure for what it is. Included in level one or may level 2 is understanding them to make it easier to hack, maybe letting you plug in. Then what? What else could the power do? Build one? Demons can't even do that. I can't see what powers you could have. <br /> <br /> Second issue. When I ran demon I had to be careful what infrastructure. A demon can take for themselves. They can anything. Powers that are as good as the ST let's it be is not great powers. I don't think they are bad just not great. Infrastructure can do anything for epic to pointless. There is no pattern to it. It's not good for anyone to have a win button that makes everything boring after. It's not good to put xp into something that doesn't do much. And the if you have a great ST that gives u cool infrastructure, it's still not great to put xp into something that will be random. U might get a room that time outside freezes while ur in there cool but a combat monster can't do much with that while a crafter it is a dream. Come to think of it most things would get more use our of that room but a vampire. Anyone else could sleep in the room, while it wouldn't help the vampire in the day. <br /> <br /> Yeah for the really mad things like a dooms day weapon that can blow up the whole world you need control of quite a few infrastructure to get that going and weird items to power it a vampire most likely can't collect. Also keeping it once u have will be hard as vampires are not the best dealing with things in twilight. Also the angel sent would be made to take down a vampire. An angel that gets fed that has blood that sets on fire when exposed to air for example wouldn't be too hard for the god machine. <br /> <br /> So what do you imagine this vampire with this power doing. Because it's cool to hack but even a human can do it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}